  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bangkok urban light song formed in the 1930s-40s around the Suntharaphon band of Eua Sunthornsanan under state cultural modernisation, and continued by Suthep Wongkamhaeng, Sawalee Phakaphan and Charin Nantanakorn into the 1960s — Western swing and foxtrot rhythms at moderate tempos played by a dance orchestra of saxophones, muted trumpet, trombone, strings, double bass and drum kit, under a smooth, vibrato-light, near-vibratoless Thai vocal that keeps clear tonal Thai diction rather than the rural nasal bends of luk thung.",
